IMPORT prelude

-- Social Residential Homes Act 2025 (Singapore, No. 14 of 2025) -- what is a licensable social residential home (s 2, s 5, First
-- Schedule), operating one without a licence (s 6), the duties on licensees over key staff (ss 17-19, penalties only), Boards of
-- Visitors (s 36(6)), force and mechanical restraints on residents (s 37), the ban on identifying residents in publications and
-- broadcasts (ss 38, 39), the limit on interim orders (s 32(3)), appeals (s 49(7)), obstructing an inspecting officer (s 45),
-- composition (s 47) and protection of informants (s 53).
--
-- Edition: the Act as enacted (No. 14 of 2025), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SRHA2025.txt. The deposit shows the
-- First Schedule as amended by S 470/2026 and the Second Schedule as amended by S 471/2026, both "wef 01/07/2026"; no later
-- amendment is annotated. The deposit's metadata says "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it is the licensing law for adult disability homes, homes for children and
-- young persons, sheltered homes for the elderly and welfare homes -- where a family member may live -- and it sets the rules on
-- restraining residents and on naming them in public. (An automated count found 2 of the 527 deposited Singapore Acts citing it by
-- title; that count undercounts and is no measure of importance.) SCOPED to the provisions a resident, a family, a member of the
-- public or a care worker meets. Not encoded: applications, grant, conditions, transfer and lapse of licences (ss 7-16), approval of
-- key staff (ss 20-23), codes of practice and directions (ss 24-26), step-in orders (Part 6), revocation and suspension (ss 30-35
-- beyond s 32(3)), enforcement powers (ss 40-44, 46), administration, corporate liability, consequential amendments and the saving
-- and transitional Schedules. Matters left to regulations ("prescribed") are taken as inputs.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Social Residential Homes Act 2025 -- homes, residents and publicity`

§§ `2, 5 and First Schedule -- what is a licensable social residential home`

-- s 2(1): "social residential home" means "any premises that are used, or intended to be used, to provide residential accommodation
-- and any one or more of the following to individuals, with or without board: (a) care; (b) biopsychosocial intervention;
-- (c) support to carry out daily activities". A "licensable SRH" is one specified in the First Schedule.
-- First Schedule para 1: (a) an adult disability home; (b) a home for children and young persons; (c) a sheltered home; (d) a welfare
-- home. Para 2:
--   "adult disability home" -- residential accommodation, care, biopsychosocial intervention, AND support to carry out daily
--     activities to an individual who "(a) is 18 years of age or older at the time of the individual's admission" and "(b) has autism
--     or any intellectual, physical or sensory disability", "but does not include any healthcare premises or premises used as a welfare
--     home";
--   "home for children and young persons" -- residential accommodation "with board and care to any child or young person for the
--     purposes of his or her protection or rehabilitation or both", excluding healthcare premises or a registered or exempt boarding
--     school; "young person" means "14 years of age or older but below 21 years of age"; "child" takes its meaning from the Children
--     and Young Persons Act 1993 (not read here, so taken as an input);
--   "sheltered home" -- residential accommodation, care and support to carry out daily activities to elderly persons ("60 years of age
--     or older"), excluding healthcare premises and premises used as an adult disability home or a welfare home;
--   "welfare home" takes its meaning from the Destitute Persons Act 1989 (not read here, so taken as an input).
-- s 5: "This Act does not apply to, or in relation to, a social residential home operated by the Government."
-- The encoding looks at the home through one resident; a home with residents of several kinds is not modelled.
DECLARE Home HAS
    `provides residential accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides board` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides biopsychosocial intervention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provides support to carry out daily activities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is healthcare premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a registered or exempt boarding school` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a welfare home under the Destitute Persons Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is operated by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident's age` IS A NUMBER
    `resident's age at admission` IS A NUMBER
    `resident has autism or an intellectual, physical or sensory disability` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resident is a child under the Children and Young Persons Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is for the resident's protection or rehabilitation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the home` IS A Home
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a social residential home` IF
    `the home`'s `provides residential accommodation`
    AND (    `the home`'s `provides care`
         OR  `the home`'s `provides biopsychosocial intervention`
         OR  `the home`'s `provides support to carry out daily activities`)

GIVEN `the home` IS A Home
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an adult disability home` IF
        `the home`'s `provides residential accommodation`
    AND `the home`'s `provides care`
    AND `the home`'s `provides biopsychosocial intervention`
    AND `the home`'s `provides support to carry out daily activities`
    AND `the home`'s `resident's age at admission` AT LEAST 18
    AND `the home`'s `resident has autism or an intellectual, physical or sensory disability`
    AND (NOT `the home`'s `is healthcare premises`)
    AND (NOT `the home`'s `is a welfare home under the Destitute Persons Act`)

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a young person` IF
    `age` AT LEAST 14 AND `age` LESS THAN 21

GIVEN `the home` IS A Home
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a home for children and young persons` IF
        `the home`'s `provides residential accommodation`
    AND `the home`'s `provides board`
    AND `the home`'s `provides care`
    AND (`the home`'s `resident is a child under the Children and Young Persons Act` OR `is a young person` (`the home`'s `resident's age`))
    AND `the home`'s `is for the resident's protection or rehabilitation`
    AND (NOT `the home`'s `is healthcare premises`)
    AND (NOT `the home`'s `is a registered or exempt boarding school`)

GIVEN `the home` IS A Home
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a sheltered home` IF
        `the home`'s `provides residential accommodation`
    AND `the home`'s `provides care`
    AND `the home`'s `provides support to carry out daily activities`
    AND `the home`'s `resident's age` AT LEAST 60
    AND (NOT `the home`'s `is healthcare premises`)
    AND (NOT `is an adult disability home` `the home`)
    AND (NOT `the home`'s `is a welfare home under the Destitute Persons Act`)

GIVEN `the home` IS A Home
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a licensable SRH` IF
        `is an adult disability home` `the home`
    OR  `is a home for children and young persons` `the home`
    OR  `is a sheltered home` `the home`
    OR  `the home`'s `is a welfare home under the Destitute Persons Act`

GIVEN `the home` IS A Home
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act's licensing applies` IF
    `is a licensable SRH` `the home` AND (NOT `the home`'s `is operated by the Government`)

§§ `6 -- operating a licensable SRH without a licence`

-- s 6(1): "A person must not operate a licensable SRH unless the person -- (a) is authorised to do so by a licence; (b) is exempt from
-- this section; or (c) is directed by the Director-General under section 26(3) to do so despite the expiry, lapse or revocation of the
-- licence". s 2(1): "operate" means to manage and maintain "in the course of business (whether or not for profit)".
-- (2): fine up to $100,000 or 2 years or both; "if the person has any previous qualifying conviction", fine up to $200,000 or 2 years
-- or both. (3): a qualifying conviction is one under s 6(2), or (whenever made) under s 4(1) or (4) of the Homes for the Aged Act 1988
-- or s 62(2) of the Children and Young Persons Act 1993, as in force before commencement.
GIVEN `the home` IS A Home, `operates it in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is exempt` IS A BOOLEAN, `directed under section 26(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `operating without authority is an offence` IF
        `the Act's licensing applies` `the home`
    AND `operates it in the course of business`
    AND (NOT `holds a licence`)
    AND (NOT `is exempt`)
    AND (NOT `directed under section 26(3)`)

DECLARE PriorConviction IS ONE OF
    `no previous conviction`
    `section 6(2) of this Act`
    `section 4(1) of the Homes for the Aged Act`
    `section 4(4) of the Homes for the Aged Act`
    `section 62(2) of the Children and Young Persons Act`
    `an unrelated offence`

GIVEN `prior` IS A PriorConviction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed operation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `prior`
    WHEN `no previous conviction` THEN 100000
    WHEN `an unrelated offence` THEN 100000
    OTHERWISE 200000

GIVEN `prior` IS A PriorConviction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for unlicensed operation` MEANS 2

§§ `17, 18, 19 -- key appointment holders, person-in-charge and deployed staff`

-- ss 17(2), 18(3), 19(1): a licensee must not allow an individual to act as a key appointment holder or as the person-in-charge, or
-- deploy an individual to carry out a prescribed duty, "except with the prior approval of the Director-General granted under
-- section 21" (and not while that approval is cancelled or suspended). ss 17(5), 18(6), 19(5): fine up to $50,000 or 12 months or both
-- "and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- offence continues after conviction". s 18(2): "there can only be one (and only one) person-in-charge".
GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unapproved staff` MEANS
    50000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `36(6) -- Boards of Visitors`

-- s 36(4), (5): a Board of Visitors reviews living conditions and the standard of care, and a member "may at any reasonable time of
-- the day enter any licensable SRH". (6): a person who "(a) refuses to allow a member of a Board of Visitors entry to any licensable
-- SRH; or (b) hinders or obstructs the member from entering any licensable SRH after the member's identity is reasonably
-- established" -- fine up to $20,000 or 12 months or both.
GIVEN `refused entry` IS A BOOLEAN, `hindered or obstructed entry` IS A BOOLEAN, `member's identity reasonably established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeping out a Board of Visitors is an offence` IF
    `refused entry` OR (`hindered or obstructed entry` AND `member's identity reasonably established`)

§§ `37 -- force and mechanical restraints on residents`

-- s 37(2): a person who carries on any duty in a licensable SRH "must not use force or any mechanical restraint on any resident".
-- (3): despite that, the person-in-charge or an authorised person may, if (a) the home is of a prescribed type; (b) the force or
-- restraint is used for a purpose in (4) "and in accordance with the prescribed manner"; (c) where force is used, no "more force than
-- is reasonable and necessary for the purpose"; and (d) the prescribed conditions (if any) are satisfied.
-- (4): to stop the resident (a) inflicting personal injury on self or others; (b) damaging property; (c) committing, attempting or
-- preparing to commit an offence; (d) contravening discipline rules; (e) "absconding from a licensable SRH that is prescribed for the
-- purposes of this paragraph". (5): it "must not also be used on the resident as punishment".
-- (7): "authorised person" is an employee of the licensee who (a) has completed any training the Director-General specifies and (b) is
-- authorised by the person-in-charge. "mechanical restraint" means "cloth bands, handcuffs, leg braces, flexi cuffs" or similar.
-- (1): the section does not limit the Penal Code. No penalty is stated in s 37 itself.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `to stop self-injury`
    `to stop injury to others`
    `to stop damage to property`
    `to stop an offence`
    `to stop a breach of discipline rules`
    `to stop absconding`
    `as punishment`
    `for staff convenience`

DECLARE Restraint HAS
    `by the person-in-charge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by an employee of the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `user completed the specified training` IS A BOOLEAN
    `user authorised by the person-in-charge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `home is prescribed for subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `home is prescribed for absconding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose` IS A Purpose
    `in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is force rather than a mechanical restraint` IS A BOOLEAN
    `more force than reasonable and necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed conditions satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `r` IS A Restraint
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the user may restrain` IF
        `r`'s `by the person-in-charge`
    OR  (    `r`'s `by an employee of the licensee`
         AND `r`'s `user completed the specified training`
         AND `r`'s `user authorised by the person-in-charge`)

GIVEN `r` IS A Restraint
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `r`'s `purpose`
    WHEN `to stop self-injury` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to stop injury to others` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to stop damage to property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to stop an offence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to stop a breach of discipline rules` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `to stop absconding` THEN `r`'s `home is prescribed for absconding`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `r` IS A Restraint
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use of force or restraint is permitted` IF
        `the user may restrain` `r`
    AND `r`'s `home is prescribed for subsection (3)`
    AND `the purpose is permitted` `r`
    AND `r`'s `in the prescribed manner`
    AND (NOT (`r`'s `is force rather than a mechanical restraint` AND `r`'s `more force than reasonable and necessary`))
    AND `r`'s `prescribed conditions satisfied`

§§ `38 -- identifying residents in publications and broadcasts`

-- s 38(1): "Except with the prior approval of the Director-General, a person must not publish or broadcast any information or picture
-- that identifies, or is likely to lead to the identification of -- (a) any resident or former resident" of a prescribed licensed SRH or
-- one of a prescribed type (a "relevant licensed SRH"), "or (b) the relevant licensed SRH at which the resident or former resident
-- resides or resided, or the location". "Publish" includes the Internet and any messaging system.
-- (2): not (a) the licensee's publication in its own publication or website; nor (b) publication "by an individual, or with the
-- consent of the individual", identifying THAT individual. (3): if the individual is below 18, consent means the consent of "the
-- individual's parent or guardian".
-- (4): every publisher, editor, distributor or broadcaster -- fine up to $5,000 or, on a second or subsequent conviction, $10,000. No
-- imprisonment.
DECLARE Publication HAS
    `identifies a resident, former resident or their home` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the home is a relevant licensed SRH` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved in advance by the Director-General` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by the licensee in its own publication or website` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identifies only the person who published it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `identified individual's age` IS A NUMBER
    `identified individual consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `parent or guardian consented` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `p` IS A Publication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is valid consent` IF
    IF `p`'s `identified individual's age` LESS THAN 18
    THEN `p`'s `parent or guardian consented`
    ELSE `p`'s `identified individual consented`

GIVEN `p` IS A Publication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publication contravenes section 38(1)` IF
        `p`'s `identifies a resident, former resident or their home`
    AND `p`'s `the home is a relevant licensed SRH`
    AND (NOT `p`'s `approved in advance by the Director-General`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `by the licensee in its own publication or website`)
    AND (NOT `p`'s `identifies only the person who published it`)
    AND (NOT `there is valid consent` `p`)

GIVEN `previous convictions under section 38` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for identifying a resident` MEANS
    IF `previous convictions under section 38` AT LEAST 1 THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

-- s 39(1): a court may, "on the application of any person", order removal, deletion or takedown. (2): it may do so even if the
-- application is not served, or the respondent does not appear, "if the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the
-- order is necessary for the protection and safety" of the resident or residents. (3): "regardless of whether the respondent or any
-- other person has been convicted". The encoding takes it (an inference) that where the respondent was served and appeared, the
-- necessity finding is not required.
GIVEN `contravenes section 38(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `respondent served and appeared` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `necessary for the protection and safety of residents` IS A BOOLEAN, `anyone convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court may order takedown` IF
    `contravenes section 38(1)` AND (`respondent served and appeared` OR `necessary for the protection and safety of residents`)

§§ `32(3), 49(7) -- interim orders and appeals`

-- s 32(3): an interim order against a licensee continues until "the expiry date (if any) stated in the interim order is reached, which
-- must not exceed 90 days", or earlier cancellation, unless confirmed. (4): before confirming, at least 7 days for representations.
GIVEN `days stated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interim order's stated duration is lawful` IF
    `days stated` AT MOST 90

-- s 49(7): an appeal "does not affect the operation of the appealable decision" and, "unless otherwise directed by the Minister", the
-- decision "must be complied with until the determination of the appeal". (5): "The Minister's decision on an appeal is final."
GIVEN `appeal pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision must be complied with now` IF
    (NOT `appeal pending`) OR (NOT `Minister directed otherwise`)

§§ `45, 47 -- obstruction and composition`

-- s 45(1), (2): wilfully preventing or obstructing an inspecting officer's entry, giving an alarm to warn others, or intentionally
-- obstructing the officer -- fine up to $20,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 47(1): the Director-General may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the
-- lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $10,000".
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    IF `prescribed as compoundable` THEN `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 10000 ELSE 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for obstructing an inspecting officer` MEANS 20000

§§ `53 -- protection of informants`

-- s 53(1): a person who "knows, or has reason to suspect, that an offence under this Act has been committed may make a notification to
-- an inspecting officer". (2)(a): by doing so the person cannot be held to have breached "any restriction on disclosure imposed by any
-- rule of law, contract or rule of professional etiquette or ethics"; (b) "insofar as the person had acted in good faith, incurs no civil
-- or criminal liability for making the notification". (3): a witness cannot be compelled to disclose the informant's identity.
GIVEN `the disclosure was a section 53 notification` IS A BOOLEAN, `the informant acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a disclosure restriction can be held against the informant` IF
    NOT `the disclosure was a section 53 notification`

GIVEN `notified an inspecting officer of a suspected offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the informant is shielded from civil and criminal liability` IF
    `notified an inspecting officer of a suspected offence` AND `acted in good faith`
